WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.108
A beautiful vesicle is not yet an inhaled medicine. The

00:00:04.108 --> 00:00:07.767
journey may fail as soon as it enters the nebulizer.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.843
An inhaled drug carrier may behave well during

00:00:19.843 --> 00:00:23.660
preparation yet fail at the first real delivery step.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.989
My master's research explores dexamethasone-loaded

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:39.237
niosomes and proniosomes, including surfactant and

00:00:39.237 --> 00:00:40.653
cholesterol composition.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.782
Particle size, formulation chemistry and loading

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:53.113
measurements belong to a reproducible analytical

00:00:53.113 --> 00:00:55.334
programme before aerosol testing.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:05.005
A vesicle must withstand aerosol generation before

00:01:05.005 --> 00:01:08.051
deposition is even a meaningful question.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.781
Particle size before aerosolisation is only a starting

00:01:20.781 --> 00:01:23.489
measurement. Compare vesicle integrity, delivery

00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:27.279
conditions and deposited fraction without assuming a

00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:27.820
result.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.192
Planned aerosol assessment asks about output,

00:01:34.192 --> 00:01:37.848
distribution and the fraction that reaches a target

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:40.590
region, not just the vial formulation.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.525
This is a research programme still being tested.

00:01:50.525 --> 00:01:54.091
Nothing here implies clinical validation of inhaled

00:01:54.091 --> 00:01:55.109
dexamethasone vesicles.
